PDF.js, vendored
================

Mozilla's PDF.js, which client.js uses to draw a paper's PDF in the panel's
browser. Apache License 2.0, see LICENSE in this folder.

Version:  6.4.299 (the modern ES module build, not the legacy one)
Source:   https://registry.npmjs.org/pdfjs-dist/-/pdfjs-dist-6.4.299.tgz
          (the pdfjs-dist package Mozilla publishes from
          https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js, tag v6.4.299)
Integrity: sha512-AVl138zALtfaAPvADulE0PZThbYzCBS79nL4pOSL/6Sm/4AH5A21BD9VHt97OlCuzJuCpmeZtAtkinisF4Vb1g==

Files, copied unchanged from the package:

  pdf.min.mjs, pdf.worker.min.mjs   from build/
  LICENSE                           the package's Apache-2.0 licence
  wasm/jbig2.wasm                   JBIG2 images (black-and-white scans), used
                                    by several US papers; without it they draw
                                    as blank boxes
  wasm/openjpeg.wasm                JPEG 2000 images
  wasm/qcms_bg.wasm, iccs/          colour management for the CMYK pages most
                                    papers send (CGATS001Compat-v2-micro.icc)
  cmaps/Adobe-*-UCS2.bcmap          the four CJK CMaps PDF.js needs to load a
                                    Chinese, Japanese or Korean CID font (the
                                    Taipei Times, for one); the other 165
                                    CMaps in the package are left out
  wasm/LICENSE_*, iccs/LICENSE,     the licences that come with those files
  cmaps/LICENSE                     (BSD, MIT, CC0)

Left out: the standard font files (standard_fonts/, for PDFs that don't embed
their fonts: none of the 54 papers checked needed them), the other CMaps, the
non-wasm fallbacks and the scripting engine, the viewer, and the source maps.

To update: download the new pdfjs-dist tarball, check its integrity against
`npm view pdfjs-dist@<version> dist.integrity`, copy the same files over, and
change the version above.
